[statement]
A package removed because a package the request brings takes a name it
provides at a version is removed at that package's turn: `icu-data-full`
takes `icu-data` from the installed `icu-data-en`, and apk removes
`icu-data-en` just before installing `icu-data-full`, after `a` and `b`,
not with `old`, which waits for nothing. Found in a layered request over
Alpine v3.24 (`liferea`'s closure installed, `kdav-dev` asked).

[repository]
P:icu-data-en
V:78.1-r0
p:icu-data=78.1-r0

P:icu-data-full
V:78.1-r0
p:icu-data=78.1-r0

P:icu-libs
V:78.1-r0
D:icu-data=78.1-r0

P:app
V:1-r0
D:a b icu-data-full

P:a
V:1-r0

P:b
V:1-r0

[installed]
P:old
V:1-r0

P:icu-data-en
V:78.1-r0
p:icu-data=78.1-r0

P:icu-libs
V:78.1-r0
D:icu-data=78.1-r0

[world]
icu-libs

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove old 1-r0
install a 1-r0
install b 1-r0
remove icu-data-en 78.1-r0
install icu-data-full 78.1-r0
install app 1-r0
